- The pin is stated once, in `crates/semantic/TSRS_VERSION`. Rust compiles it into `SUPPORTED_VERSIONS`, and `scripts/check-packaging.mjs` (part of `just lint`) fails unless all 10 platform manifests and the oracle's `tsrs` match it exactly (a mutated pin made it fail). Dependabot now ignores `tsrs` and `@tsrs/*`, because a pin change needs the tsrs-versus-Go parity run (ADR 0026).
- Resolution is one function, `find_tsc` in `crates/semantic/src/locate.rs`, used by the CLI and by napi. Order: (1) `--tsc-path` or `tscPath`; (2) `@tsrs/<platform>/tsrs[.exe]` in the nearest `node_modules` above the running binary (gnu or musl decided at build time; the CLI finds itself through `current_exe`, napi through `node_api_get_module_file_name`, napi9); (3) the project's `typescript/bin/tsc`, then `tsrs/bin/tsrs`. There is no environment variable. If nothing is found, one `SEMANTIC_BACKEND` warning names the package, the directory searched and what to install.
- Behaviour change for opt-in users: the bundled tsrs now wins over a project's own `typescript@beta`. The changeset says so. New public field `binary_dir: Result<Utf8PathBuf, String>` on `SemanticRequest` and `OnDemandConfig`, so `caliper-docgen-semantic` gets a minor version.

## Size per platform (registry tarballs, packed and unpacked)

- darwin-arm64 10.5 and 23.9 MB; darwin-x64 11.1 and 25.4; linux-x64-gnu 15.4 and 35.2; linux-arm64-gnu 20.4 and 43.4; win32-x64 20.2 and 50.2. There is no win32-arm64 package.

